## std.argv — command-line argument access.
##
## From docs/spec.md §6.4 (System Surfaces): argv is exposed as a
## free-fn form after the user writes `pub import std.argv.{get}`.
## The router in src/codegen/builtins.zig fires on a `get()` call and
## emits a per-call `(blk: { var __argv_<N>: [32][]const u8 = undefined;
## ...; break :blk __argv_<N>[0..__argv_<N>_n]; })` wrapper that captures
## `std.os.argv` into a stack-allocated 32-slot slice bounded by the
## walk count `__argv_<N>_n`. The emit uses `std.mem.span(a)` directly
## (no `orelse ""` wrapper) because `std.os.argv` on Linux stores
## non-optional sentinel-terminated pointers — `orelse` would have
## hard-errored at compile time per Phase 0's Linux-correctness work.
##
## Stub: throwaway body so the .zag file parses through the existing
## stub convention; the genBuiltinCall arm REWRITES the call site
## before any reader sees the verbatim form.

pub fun get() -> []const []const u8 {
    var empty: [0][]const u8 = undefined;
    return empty[0..0];
}
